From 3ef96fc324cdfd2ecc10f02ca97323d9983f0dad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:15:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] refactor(mailbox): move IMAP server and incoming client
 to go-imap/v2

v1's server is in maintenance and its backend interface has no model for
unilateral updates beyond a raw channel, which is why the previous commit had
to hand-build the plumbing that pushes new mail to idling clients. v2 provides
that properly, so both the server and the incoming client move to it and v1
leaves the tree.

Server, rewritten on the imapserver.Session interface:
- IDLE and NOOP polling are backed by MailboxTracker/SessionTracker instead of
  the hand-rolled update channel, which also gives each connection a stable
  view of sequence numbers so an expunge elsewhere cannot shift the numbering a
  command is working through
- MOVE is now native rather than leaving clients to emulate it with
  COPY + STORE + EXPUNGE
- adds IMAP4rev2, NAMESPACE, UIDPLUS, ESEARCH, LIST-EXTENDED, LIST-STATUS and
  STATUS=SIZE, and reports RFC 6154 special-use attributes so clients can find
  Sent, Drafts, Trash, Archive and Junk without guessing from names
- SEARCH is evaluated against the columns extracted at delivery time rather
  than reparsing each message, and FETCH still loads raw bytes only for the
  items that need them

One tracker is kept per folder that has a session selected on it and dropped
when the last one leaves, so an idle instance holds no per-folder state.

Incoming client moves to imapclient: the mailbox-update handler is registered
in the dial options and signals the idle loop, replacing v1's Updates channel.
UID-based search, fetch and store replace the sequence-number variants, which
removes a race where an expunge between search and fetch could shift the
numbers the client had just been given.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
